CREATED:19000101T120000Z
DESCRIPTION:Saints\, Feasts\, and Readings for 03/15/2025\n\nSaints and Fea
 sts: Second Saturday of Lent\; Agapius the Martyr & His Companions\; Manuel
  the New Martyr of Crete\; Holy Apostle Aristobulos of the Seventy\, Bishop
  of Britain\n\nFast Day (Wine and Oil Allowed)\n\nEpistle Reading: Hebrews 
 3:12-16\nBRETHREN\, take care lest there be in any of you an evil\, unbelie
 ving heart\, leading you to fall away from the living God. But exhort one a
 nother every day\, as long as it is called "today\," that none of you may b
 e hardened by the deceitfulness of sin. For we share in Christ\, if only we
  hold our first confidence firm to the end\, while it is said\, "Today\, wh
 en you hear his voice\, do not harden your hearts as in the rebellion." Who
  were they that heard and yet were rebellious? Was it not all those who lef
 t Egypt under the leadership of Moses? \n\nGospel Reading: Mark 1:35-44\nAt
  that time\, Jesus went out to a lonely place\, and there he prayed. And Si
 mon and those who were with him pursued him\, and they found him and said t
 o him\, "Everyone is searching for you." And he said to them\, "Let us go o
 n to the next towns\, that I may preach there also\; for that is why I came
  out." And he went throughout all Galilee\, preaching in their synagogues a
 nd casting out demons. And a leper came to him beseeching him\, and kneelin
 g said to him\, "If you will\, you can make me clean." Moved with pity\, he
  stretched out his hand and touched him\, and said to him\, "I will\; be cl
 ean." And immediately the leprosy left him\, and he was made clean. And he 
 sternly charged him\, and sent him away at once\, and said to him\, "See th
 at you say nothing to any one\; but go\, show yourself to a priest\, and of
 fer for your cleansing what Moses commanded\, for a proof to them."\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20240730T001057Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:🍇 Second Saturday of Lent
TRANSP:OPAQUE
