UID:474f41524348-456e676c697368-20270327
CREATED:20260810T222328Z
DESCRIPTION:Saints\, Feasts\, and Readings for 03/27/2027\n\nSaints and Fea
 sts: Second Saturday of Lent\; Martyr Matrona of Thessalonica\; Paul\, Bish
 op of Corinth\n\nFast Day (Wine and Oil Allowed)\n\nEpistle Reading: Hebrew
 s 3:12-16\nBRETHREN\, take care lest there be in any of you an evil\, unbel
 ieving heart\, leading you to fall away from the living God. But exhort one
  another every day\, as long as it is called "today\," that none of you may
  be hardened by the deceitfulness of sin. For we share in Christ\, if only 
 we hold our first confidence firm to the end\, while it is said\, "Today\, 
 when you hear his voice\, do not harden your hearts as in the rebellion." W
 ho were they that heard and yet were rebellious? Was it not all those who l
 eft Egypt under the leadership of Moses? \n\nGospel Reading: Mark 1:35-44\n
 At that time\, Jesus went out to a lonely place\, and there he prayed. And 
 Simon and those who were with him pursued him\, and they found him and said
  to him\, "Everyone is searching for you." And he said to them\, "Let us go
  on to the next towns\, that I may preach there also\; for that is why I ca
 me out." And he went throughout all Galilee\, preaching in their synagogues
  and casting out demons. And a leper came to him beseeching him\, and kneel
 ing said to him\, "If you will\, you can make me clean." Moved with pity\, 
 he stretched out his hand and touched him\, and said to him\, "I will\; be 
 clean." And immediately the leprosy left him\, and he was made clean. And h
 e sternly charged him\, and sent him away at once\, and said to him\, "See 
 that you say nothing to any one\; but go\, show yourself to a priest\, and 
 offer for your cleansing what Moses commanded\, for a proof to them."\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T202310Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:🍇 Second Saturday of Lent
